{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 83,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A song, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Psalm of Asaph. Keep not thou silence, O God: hold not thy peace, and be not still, O God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For lo, thy enemies make a tumult: and they that hate thee have lifted up the head.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have taken crafty counsel against thy people, and consulted against thy hidden ones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have said, Come, and let us cut them off from ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a nation; that the name of Israel may be no more in remembrance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they have consulted together with one consent: they are confederate against thee,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The tabernacles of Edom, and the Ishmaelites; of Moab, and the Hagarenes;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek; the Philistines with the inhabitants of Tyre;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Assur also is joined with them: they have helped the children of Lot. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do to them as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Midianites; as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Sisera, as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Jabin, at the brook of Kison:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perished at En-dor: they became ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " dung for the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make their nobles like Oreb, and like Zeeb: yes, all their princes as Zebah, and as Zalmunna:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who said, Let us take to ourselves the houses of God in possession.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O my God, make them like a wheel; as the stubble before the wind.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As the fire burneth a wood, and as the flame setteth the mountains on fire;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So persecute them with thy tempest, and make them afraid with thy storm.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fill their faces with shame; that they may seek thy name, O LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them be confounded and troubled for ever; yes, let them be put to shame, and perish:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.83.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " may know that thou, whose name alone ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " JEHOVAH, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the most high over all the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
